From 90e33bacf813c689f9980ce59efb978f85cf1cc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:33:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Draw engine: main-memory colour targets coherent with
 guest memory (PS3RECOMP_ENG_MAIN_COHERENCE); sampling diagnostics

PS3RECOMP_ENG_MAIN_COHERENCE=1: at each label release (NV406E release,
NV4097 back-end release) the main-memory colour targets drawn since are
stored to guest memory, so the CPU and SPUs that read them after syncing
on the label see what the RSX drew; a target sampled after its guest bytes
changed (an SPU wrote them) is uploaded first. Off by default.
RSX_ENGINE_SAMPLE_LOG=<n>: the first n binds of a colour target as a
texture. RSX_ENGINE_MAIN_TEX_LOG=1: each main-memory texture bound, once.
Killzone HD, Level 7: the RSX samples only its two 640x360 main-memory
targets (IO 0x10000, 0xF1000), ~150 times a second each; the SPU post
chain reads them and writes elsewhere (IO 0x1D2000, 0x556000...), which
nothing samples.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
